---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import QuoteCta from '../../components/QuoteCta.astro';
import ServiceCard from '../../components/ServiceCard.astro';
import { SERVICES } from '../../data/catalog';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/schema';

const schema = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Services', path: '/services/' },
]);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Printing Services: Offset, Digital & Design"
  description="Offset for identical runs, digital when each piece can differ, and design help from a logo. Free quotes, a proof before print, shipped in the US."
  schema={schema}
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Services"
    title="Printing services built around your project"
    subtitle="Offset or digital, a file that is ready, a free quote, and a proof before it prints."
  />

  <!-- Copy: Content Strategist's thin-pages-copy.md. -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pt-9">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <Prose>
        <p>
          Offset or digital is a choice about the pieces, not a menu you have to
          decode. <a href="/services/offset-printing/">Offset printing</a> is for
          a run of identical pieces whose color has to match from the first sheet
          to the last. A brochure, a flyer, or a catalog can look the same in the
          first carton and the last. <a href="/services/digital-printing/"
            >Digital printing</a
          > puts the image on the sheet from the file, with no plate. One card can
          carry a different name. One mailer can carry a different offer. You do not
          have to pick the press. Tell us the product, how many you need, and whether
          every piece is the same. The quote names the process.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/services/graphic-design/">Graphic design and prepress</a> comes
          before either press. A press-ready file can go straight to a proof. A logo
          and a rough layout are enough for us to build the file, with bleed, type,
          and the cuts where they belong. The quote is free. Nothing prints until
          you approve the proof. We then ship the job anywhere in the United States.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pt-10 pb-14 md:pt-12 md:pb-18">
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      {
        SERVICES.map((service) => (
          <ServiceCard service={service} headingLevel={2} />
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <QuoteCta />
</BaseLayout>
